A||||4||Gokart||Oil pump time?||||5||
Z||000000||Gokart||07-12-2000||06:08 AM||||Noticed lately that my oil pressure wasn't what it used to be. When idleing it barely stays over the red mark on my gauge. When reving it only hits 55/60. Time for a new pump? Who makes the best replacement and is it an easy job? I've already removed the oil pan once before so I know what a headache that is! <P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||dogtired||07-12-2000||06:25 AM||||GoKart, Hope you get some good replies  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Last time I ask the same question, with just a little twist. My oil pressure seemed OK just a little low but when I would turn on the AC it would drop to the panic point  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> RED light and all.<BR>The response I got was that it was time for an overhaul because the motor is so worn that it will no longer hold proper pressure under a load   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>I was thinking about maybe a ? HIGH VOLUME, High output Oil pump that maybe it would give my motor the extra pressure to operate the AC?? The motor I am speaking of only has 85000 miles on it and no smoke and seems like plenty of power?? Just low but acceptible oil pressure without AC?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Just thought I would jump in here and see if others may have an idea that would help us both  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||6
Z||000002||batboy||07-12-2000||07:18 AM||||It could be that the oil pump is getting worn out, but usually it's the crank and rod bearings getting worn that causes low pressure or a combination of both.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Taijiguy||07-12-2000||08:16 AM||||If it were me, I'd be suspecting the motor is getting loose. You could put a hi pressure, hi volume pump in it, but that's just a band aid to briefly hold off the inevitible. (You could also just use heavier grade oil) I'd plasti-gage the bearings while I have the pan off, and see how much gap there is, and replace 'em if they aren't nice and tight. Good luck wit' dat job!||||reg||1
Z||000004||peterh||07-12-2000||10:08 AM||||I have low oil pressure also at hot idle on my 86SE V6 with 122,000 miles. I put in 10w40 in with 1 qt of 20w50 and the oil pressure stays out of the red even with airconditioning on. A high pressure of "only" 55 is actually normal when cruising. Try a heavier oil and see if this helps.<BR>||||reg||1
